<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<div>
  <p>
    <strong>Parameter Foundry</strong> provides one parameter model for choices and typed input
    across the Jenkins UI, Pipeline, REST, CLI, webhooks, upstream builds, and Rebuild. Every entry
    point calls the same server-side evaluation service, so the value a user picks is the value the
    build records.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Foundry Choice Parameter</strong> — single selection, multiple selection, and
      two-dimensional choice tables, with inline or Provider-backed options and reactive refresh.</li>
    <li><strong>Foundry Form Parameter</strong> — typed schema with validation, layouts,
      conditional visibility, canonical JSON output, and governed environment export.</li>
    <li>Renderers: select, searchable, radio, list, checkbox, chips, table, and a packaged
      accessible choice grid.</li>
    <li>Providers: static, managed configuration, REST (JSON and XML), sandboxed Groovy, and Git
      refs, all behind governed Connection Profiles. Migration adapters cover Active Choices,
      Extended Choice, List Git Branches, and other source parameter families.</li>
    <li>The core plugin never executes Job-supplied Groovy, JavaScript, or HTML, and never reads
      controller file paths.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Open the question mark next to any configuration field for field-level help. The user guide
    (getting started, parameter reference, cookbook, providers, migration, best practices,
    troubleshooting) lives in <code>docs/guide/</code> in the plugin repository.
  </p>
</div>
